# 14. Interim Applications—Common Types

**Authors:** Lucilla Macgregor, Charlotte Peacey, Georgina Ridsdale

## Abstract
<p>This chapter considers the interim applications that a legal representative may most often come across in practice. It looks at the procedure for the specific interim application. Then it discusses the form of the evidence needed to make or oppose it. The interim applications considered here include an application to set aside default judgment; summary judgment; interim payment; an application for specific disclosure; an application for security for costs; and an application for an injunction.</p>

**Source:** https://doi.org/10.1093/he/9780192844293.003.0014

